[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71364,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic small round cell tumour (DSRCT) is a malignant mesenchymal neoplasm composed of small round tumour cells associated with prominent stromal desmoplasia, polyphenotypic differentiation, and <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>WT1</em> gene fusion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71365,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8806/3 Desmoplastic small round cell tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71366,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5F.2 &amp; XH5SN6 Sarcoma, not elsewhere classified of other specified sites &amp; Desmoplastic small round cell tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71367,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> polyphenotypic small round cell tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71368,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71369,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common genitourinary site for DSRCT is the paratestis {9042290}. Rarely, it occurs in the kidney {32804706}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71370,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with paratesticular tumours present with a palpable mass. Patients with kidney tumours present with haematuria or flank pain. Spread to the intra-abdominal cavity is common.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71371,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DSRCT primarily affects children and young adults {9042290; 1709557}, with a striking male predominance. Peak incidence is in the third decade of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71372,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71373,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DSRCTs harbour a t(11;22)(p13;q12) translocation, resulting in <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>WT1</em> fusion {8187063; 1314522}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71374,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DSRCTs typically have a multilobulated appearance with a white to grey fleshy cut surface. Cystic change and necrosis may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71375,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "<p>DSRCT is characterized by sharply outlined nests of uniform small cells with scant cytoplasm embedded in a prominent desmoplastic stroma. The nests vary considerably in size, ranging from minute clusters to large, irregular, confluent sheets. Other histological patterns include epithelioid, rhabdoid, corded, pseudopapillary, and spindled morphology. Rare cases may show epithelial features (glands or a rosette pattern) or cellular pleomorphism. Mitoses are frequent and individual cell necrosis is common. The desmoplastic stroma is composed of fibroblasts or myofibroblasts embedded in a loose extracellular matrix or collagen.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemically, DSRCT has an unusual multiphenotypic expression pattern with reactivity for markers of epithelial, muscle, and neural differentiation. Most cases are immunoreactive for cytokeratins, EMA, and desmin {9738572}. Distinctive dot-like cytoplasmic immunoreactivity is seen for desmin and sometimes for keratin. Rare cases may not coexpress cytokeratin and desmin. Myogenin and MYOD1 are consistently negative. Nuclear expression of WT1 (using antibodies to the C-terminus but not the N-terminus) is typical {10843285; 10989634}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-05-03T15:57:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71376,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71377,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The presence of <em>EWSR1</em> and <em>WT1</em> gene rearrangements or the <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>WT1</em> chimeric transcript is characteristic {7862627; 7495283; 1314522}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71378,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> sharply defined nests of small round tumour cells (epithelioid or rhabdoid cells in some cases) associated with prominent stromal desmoplasia and coexpression of cytokeratin and desmin.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>EWSR1</em> and <em>WT1</em> gene rearrangement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71379,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Soft tissue sarcoma staging is applicable.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71380,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Spread to the intra-abdominal cavity is common, and the prognosis is poor {25440720}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:52:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]